# Prism.js already included via CDN in docs pages
```

## Architecture Patterns

### Recommended Project Structure

Current flat structure needs reorganization to `/projects/graphics-engine/` hierarchy:

```
/
├── index.html                              # Portfolio landing page
├── projects/
│   └── graphics-engine/
│       ├── demo.html                       # Interactive demo (currently graphics-demo.html)
│       ├── wasm-demo.html                  # WebAssembly demo (currently wasm-graphics-demo.html)
│       ├── admin.html                      # Source code viewer
│       └── docs/
│           ├── index.html                  # Documentation landing
│           ├── core-rendering.html
│           ├── transforms-textures.html
│           ├── paths-gradients.html
│           ├── advanced-geometry.html
│           ├── optimization-performance.html
│           ├── final-features.html
│           ├── api-reference.html
│           ├── architecture.html
│           ├── implementation.html
│           └── assets/
│               ├── css/
│               │   ├── docs.css
│               │   ├── code.css
│               │   └── design-system.css   # NEW: shared design tokens
│               └── js/
│                   └── navigation.js       # NEW: mobile menu logic
```

### Pattern 1: Design Token System

**What:** CSS Custom Properties for all design values (colors, spacing, typography)

**When to use:** Essential for maintaining consistency across portfolio and project pages

**Example:**
```css
/* design-system.css - Shared across all pages */
:root {
  /* Colors - Green palette (unified) */
  --color-primary: #2E7D32;
  --color-primary-dark: #1B5E20;
  --color-primary-light: #4CAF50;

  --color-neutral-900: #2c3e50;
  --color-neutral-800: #34495e;
  --color-neutral-100: #f8f9fa;
  --color-neutral-50: #ffffff;

  --color-accent: #667eea;
  --color-accent-dark: #5568d3;

  /* Typography - Fluid scaling */
  --font-size-base: clamp(1rem, 0.9rem + 0.5vw, 1.125rem);
  --font-size-h1: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2vw, 3rem);
  --font-size-h2: clamp(1.5rem, 1.25rem + 1vw, 2rem);
  --font-size-h3: clamp(1.25rem, 1.125rem + 0.5vw, 1.5rem);
  --font-size-small: clamp(0.875rem, 0.85rem + 0.25vw, 0.95rem);

  /* Spacing - 8px base scale */
  --space-xs: 0.5rem;   /* 8px */
  --space-sm: 1rem;     /* 16px */
  --space-md: 1.5rem;   /* 24px */
  --space-lg: 2rem;     /* 32px */
  --space-xl: 3rem;     /* 48px */
  --space-2xl: 4rem;    /* 64px */

  /* Layout */
  --max-width-content: 1200px;
  --max-width-text: 800px;
  --border-radius: 8px;
  --border-radius-lg: 12px;

  /* Transitions */
  --transition-fast: 0.15s ease;
  --transition-base: 0.2s ease;
  --transition-slow: 0.3s ease;

  /* Shadows */
  --shadow-sm: 0 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
  --shadow-md: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  --shadow-lg: 0 10px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
}

/* Usage example */
.project-card {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-primary) 0%, var(--color-primary-dark) 100%);
  padding: var(--space-lg);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  transition: transform var(--transition-base);
}
```

### Pattern 2: Fluid Typography with clamp()

**What:** Smooth font size scaling between minimum and maximum using CSS clamp() with rem + vw

**When to use:** All text that needs to scale between mobile and desktop

**Example:**
```css
/* Accessibility-safe fluid typography */
/* Formula: clamp(min-size, preferred-size, max-size) */
/* Preferred size uses calc(base-rem + viewport-factor) for zoom support */

body {
  /* Base: 16px mobile → 18px desktop */
  font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.9rem + 0.5vw, 1.125rem);
  line-height: 1.6;
}

h1 {
  /* Large headers: 32px mobile → 48px desktop */
  font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2vw, 3rem);
  line-height: 1.2;
  margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
}

h2 {
  /* Medium headers: 24px mobile → 32px desktop */
  font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.25rem + 1vw, 2rem);
  line-height: 1.3;
}

/* Code blocks - fixed size for alignment */
code, pre {
  font-family: 'Cascadia Code', 'Fira Code', 'Monaco', 'Courier New', monospace;
  font-size: 0.875rem; /* Fixed size for code alignment */
}
```

**Critical accessibility note:** Pure vw units don't respect browser zoom. Always combine vw with rem in calc() for the preferred value.

### Pattern 3: Consistent Card System with CSS Grid

**What:** Unified card design with CSS Grid + subgrid for alignment across varying content

**When to use:** Portfolio projects, documentation page cards, feature lists

**Example:**
```css
/* Card grid container */
.card-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(300px, 100%), 1fr));
  gap: var(--space-lg);
  margin: var(--space-xl) 0;
}

/* Unified card styling */
.card {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-primary) 0%, var(--color-primary-dark) 100%);
  color: var(--color-neutral-50);
  padding: var(--space-lg);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  transition: transform var(--transition-base), box-shadow var(--transition-base);

  /* Subgrid for internal alignment */
  display: grid;
  grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto;
  gap: var(--space-sm);
}

.card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-4px);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
}

.card-title {
  font-size: var(--font-size-h3);
  font-weight: 700;
  margin: 0;
}

.card-description {
  margin: 0;
  opacity: 0.95;
  line-height: 1.6;
}

.card-actions {
  display: flex;
  gap: var(--space-sm);
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-top: var(--space-sm);
}
```

### Pattern 4: Accessible Hamburger Menu Navigation

**What:** Mobile-first drawer navigation with proper ARIA attributes and keyboard support

**When to use:** Mobile viewports (< 768px) for complex navigation hierarchies

**Example:**
```html
