   189→
   190→### Pattern 2: Fluid Typography with clamp()
   191→
   192→**What:** Smooth font size scaling between minimum and maximum using CSS clamp() with rem + vw
   193→
   194→**When to use:** All text that needs to scale between mobile and desktop
   195→
   196→**Example:**
   197→```css
   198→/* Accessibility-safe fluid typography */
   199→/* Formula: clamp(min-size, preferred-size, max-size) */
   200→/* Preferred size uses calc(base-rem + viewport-factor) for zoom support */
   201→
   202→body {
   203→  /* Base: 16px mobile → 18px desktop */
   204→  font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.9rem + 0.5vw, 1.125rem);
   205→  line-height: 1.6;
   206→}
   207→
   208→h1 {
   209→  /* Large headers: 32px mobile → 48px desktop */
   210→  font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2vw, 3rem);
   211→  line-height: 1.2;
   212→  margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
   213→}
   214→
   215→h2 {
   216→  /* Medium headers: 24px mobile → 32px desktop */
   217→  font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.25rem + 1vw, 2rem);
   218→  line-height: 1.3;
   219→}
   220→
   221→/* Code blocks - fixed size for alignment */
   222→code, pre {
   223→  font-family: 'Cascadia Code', 'Fira Code', 'Monaco', 'Courier New', monospace;
   224→  font-size: 0.875rem; /* Fixed size for code alignment */
   225→}
   226→```
   227→
   228→**Critical accessibility note:** Pure vw units don't respect browser zoom. Always combine vw with rem in calc() for the preferred value.
