   313→            <h2>About the 2D Graphics Engine</h2>
   314→
   315→            <h3>What is this?</h3>
   316→            <p>
   317→                This is a <strong>2D graphics API</strong> similar to OpenGL, but focused on 2D rendering instead of 3D. Just like OpenGL provides functions for drawing triangles and applying textures in 3D space, this engine provides a complete API for 2D drawing operations.
   318→            </p>
   319→            <p>
   320→                It's a software renderer built from scratch in C++, implementing functionality found in production libraries like <strong>Skia</strong> (used by Chrome and Android), <strong>Cairo</strong> (used by GTK and Firefox), and the <strong>HTML5 Canvas API</strong>. You give it high-level drawing commands—"draw a rectangle," "fill a path with a gradient," "apply a matrix transformation"—and it produces the actual pixel colors on screen.
   321→            </p>
   322→            <p>
   323→                <strong>Key Features:</strong>
   324→            </p>
   325→            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: #555;">
   326→                <li><strong>Shape Drawing:</strong> Rectangles, polygons, paths with curves</li>
   327→                <li><strong>Transformations:</strong> 2D affine matrices (translate, rotate, scale) with CTM stack</li>
   328→                <li><strong>Shaders:</strong> Solid colors, linear/radial/sweep gradients, bitmap textures with tile modes</li>
   329→                <li><strong>Compositing:</strong> Porter-Duff blend modes (12 modes including src-over, xor, multiply)</li>
   330→                <li><strong>Path Rendering:</strong> Winding fill rule, Bezier curve tessellation</li>
   331→                <li><strong>Advanced Geometry:</strong> Triangle meshes, Coons patches, shader composition</li>
   332→            </ul>
   333→
   334→            <h3>Technologies Used</h3>
   335→            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: #555;">
   336→                <li><strong>C++17:</strong> Core rendering engine implementation with hand-optimized rasterization algorithms</li>
   337→                <li><strong>WebAssembly:</strong> Compiles C++ to bytecode that runs at near-native speed in the browser</li>
   338→                <li><strong>Emscripten:</strong> Toolchain for compiling C++ to WebAssembly and generating JavaScript bindings</li>
   339→                <li><strong>HTML5 Canvas API:</strong> Display target for the rendered pixel buffer (ARGB → RGBA at 60fps)</li>
   340→            </ul>
   341→
   342→            <h3>The Rendering Pipeline</h3>
   343→            <p>
   344→                Every draw call flows through this pipeline, transforming high-level commands into pixel colors:
   345→            </p>
   346→
   347→            <div class="pipeline-diagram">
   348→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   349→                    <h4>Draw Call</h4>
   350→                    <p>High-level command</p>
   351→                </div>
   352→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   353→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   354→                    <h4>Transform</h4>
   355→                    <p>Apply CTM matrix</p>
   356→                </div>
   357→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   358→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   359→                    <h4>Clip</h4>
   360→                    <p>Constrain to viewport</p>
   361→                </div>
   362→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   363→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   364→                    <h4>Rasterize</h4>
   365→                    <p>Edges to pixels</p>
   366→                </div>
   367→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   368→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   369→                    <h4>Shade</h4>
   370→                    <p>Compute color</p>
   371→                </div>
   372→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   373→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   374→                    <h4>Blend</h4>
   375→                    <p>Composite layers</p>
   376→                </div>
   377→                <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
   378→                <div class="pipeline-step">
   379→                    <h4>Pixels</h4>
   380→                    <p>Final framebuffer</p>
   381→                </div>
   382→            </div>
